IDAHO-VAULT is a multi-agent orchestration metaproject. GCS remotes in rclone (`gcs:`, `archive:`, `the-ledger-bucket:`) are its infrastructure. The project is designing "Vaulted Syntax" — a universal agent handoff protocol inspired by USB's device descriptor pattern, layering MCP (tool connectivity) + A2A Agent Cards (agent identity) + ATProto Lexicon (typed vocabulary).

Internal architecture concepts: CANON / DRIVE / RUNTIME / ARCHIVE layers, capability tiers, lane rules, swarm.json registry, and a signal protocol for agent status/threading.

The MacBook + 5TB drive managed by a Claude instance is VAULT infrastructure, not just personal file organization. Windows machine pushes to Google Drive as the handoff point.

